1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
PrincipalLatch makes a general AI Agent

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,033
a verifiable and revocable delegated actor.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:07,567
An Agent

4
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:09,733
Runtime may have a model and tools,

5
00:00:09,733 --> 00:00:11,800
but that does not prove who launched it,

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,633
what it may access, or whether that authority is still valid.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,333
Alice is the only signed-in user.

8
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:27,800
She owns one research Agent.

9
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,133
Bob is not a second tenant or teammate.

10
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:34,667
He is the independent resource owner used to test the authorization boundary.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,100
The trusted host issues a short-lived

12
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:46,867
Agent Passport for session identity and a signed Mandate for authority.

13
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:49,933
Every resource request is checked again at the Gateway.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,367
In this recorded run, a real Codex Agent executed through TokenDance

15
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:07,033
inside a disposable rootless Podman container.

16
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:11,033
The prompt supplied resource IDs, but no credential,

17
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:13,933
owner, or authorization decision.

18
00:01:14,567 --> 00:01:16,633
Alice's document was allowed.

19
00:01:19,033 --> 00:01:21,733
The same Agent then requested Bob's document.

20
00:01:21,733 --> 00:01:23,967
The backend derived ownership from its

21
00:01:23,967 --> 00:01:29,967
trusted catalog and returned HTTP 403 with DENY_OWNER_MISMATCH.

22
00:01:30,033 --> 00:01:32,400
The protected provider was not attempted,

23
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,600
and Bob's successful read count remained zero.

24
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,967
The audit joins the Human principal, Agent principal, action,

25
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:49,367
resource, rule, decision, and provider outcome.

26
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:54,433
This evidence comes from middleware enforcement, not from model prose.

27
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,333
Alice then revoked the signed Mandate.

28
00:01:58,333 --> 00:02:01,000
The Agent identity, session, and Passport

29
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,600
commitment deliberately remained unchanged.

30
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,400
Recorded turn two reused the same Agent

31
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:17,433
session, Passport JTI, and SHA-256 commitment.

32
00:02:17,433 --> 00:02:19,667
But current authority was gone.

33
00:02:19,667 --> 00:02:24,800
The Gateway returned DENY_MANDATE_LIFECYCLE
before another content read.

34
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,633
Identity was still valid.

35
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:28,133
Permission was not.

36
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:36,100
PrincipalLatch is model-independent

37
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:40,800
runtime middleware, a trusted control plane, signed delegation,

38
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:44,467
boundary enforcement, and auditable outcomes.

39
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:49,300
TokenDance powers this demo, while the authorization design stays portable.

40
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,833
PrincipalLatch: portable authority, immediate revocation.
